.TH SWARM-INFO 1 "August 2026" "swarm-info 1.17.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swarm-info \- inspect Docker Swarm health and image vulnerabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swarm-info
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swarm-info
runs its full information tour on a Docker Swarm manager. With no arguments on
a standalone Docker host it instead starts the compatible local-container
security check. The explicit
.B \-\-security-check
compatibility command also supports standalone Linux Docker hosts and QNAP
Container Station without activating Swarm.
.PP
Vulnerability scans are explicit because an all-image scan can take several
minutes and may use registry bandwidth. Missing, incomplete, or stale evidence
is never reported as clean.
.SH OPERATOR PAGES
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-service-health
Show only down or degraded services and investigation commands.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vulnerabilities
Show the latest vulnerability evidence and image-specific remediation
commands. In an interactive terminal, a vulnerable report continues into the
guided remediation menu. Add
.B \-\-menu
to scan immediately or refresh the page.
.TP
.B \-\-map-service-deployments
Render candidate YAML through Docker Compose and map each live service to one
unique owning stack file. Missing stack names require exact live service/image
consensus. Source-image drift and defaults-only fallback rendering are marked
unverified and cannot authorize automatic source editing. The command is
read-only, reports conflicting evidence as ambiguous, and exits with status 2
while any path or source remains unverified.
.TP
.B \-\-remediate-vulnerabilities
Open the interactive remediation workflow. It offers targeted service and
image guidance, priority-ordered guidance, conservative built-in
auto-remediation, and installation-policy overrides. A missing policy no
longer aborts: swarm-info creates an inert generated review queue. Built-in
execution is limited to a validated same-major digest change for a verified
source already following latest, with separate default-No backup/compatibility
and update confirmations. All other items remain blocked until reviewed policy
targets authorize them. No mutation is available without a terminal, fresh
complete scan, current manager access, exact rollback evidence, and separate
confirmations.
.PP
Targeted guidance first asks the operator to open a second terminal. It runs
read-only Scout and image-metadata checks with a progress heartbeat. Standard
image labels or explicit tags identify the current application release when
available. A digest alone is not treated as historical version metadata.
Scout base-image refreshes are shown only as rebuild guidance. An immutable
policy candidate, or a newly resolved digest behind
.BR latest ,
is placed in update commands only after the same no-new-findings and
risk-improvement validation used by automatic remediation. Visible version
metadata also distinguishes a same-major proposal from a possible breaking
major upgrade. Set
.B NO_COLOR=1
to disable interactive ANSI emphasis.
.SH INVENTORY OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-basic
Show basic Swarm information.
.TP
.BR \-\-services
Show service inventory and the service-health summary.
.TP
.BR \-\-node-services
Show services grouped by node.
.TP
.BR \-\-stacks
Show stack inventory.
.TP
.BR \-\-stack-services
Show services grouped by stack.
.TP
.BR \-\-network
Show Swarm networks.
.B \-\-net
is an alias.
.TP
.BR \-\-secrets
Show secret metadata without secret values.
.TP
.BR \-\-labels
Show node labels.
.TP
.BR \-\-local
Show local Docker information.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-commands
Show the curated Docker and Swarm command reference.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image-cleanup
Review images unused on the current Docker node. Running and stopped container
images are protected. A manager also protects locally available images declared
by any Swarm service. Swarm workers are read-only because they lack complete
service visibility.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
With
.BR \-\-image-cleanup ,
request removal after a default-No confirmation and a fresh safety inventory.
Parent chains needed by protected images remain protected. Approved unused
branches are removed child-first, dependency conflicts are retried after
progress, and multi-tag images require an exact tag-to-image recheck before
untagging. Docker's force option is never used.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With
.BR "\-\-image-cleanup \-\-apply" ,
confirm removal non-interactively. Only reviewed exact artifacts and their
revalidated tags are removed, without force.
.TP
.B \-\-state
Check whether the installed swarm-info checkout is current and modified.
.SH REPORT AND SCAN OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Collect and atomically publish the Swarm health JSON report.
.TP
.BI \-o " path" ", " \-\-output-file " path"
Select the health, vulnerability, image-update, deployment-map, or image-cleanup report
destination.
.TP
.BI \-\-deploy-root " path"
Set an absolute directory searched recursively by deployment mapping. Repeat
the option for multiple roots. Default: /swarm. The
.B SWARM_INFO_DEPLOY_ROOTS
environment variable provides a path-separated default.
.TP
.BI \-\-deployment-map-file " path"
Load a previously reviewed deployment-map JSON for guidance. Auto-remediation
regenerates live mapping evidence before it plans any mutation.
.TP
.BI \-\-remediation-policy " path"
Select an installation-owned JSON policy containing exact services, immutable
candidate images, backup classifications, and optional source adapters. In
automatic mode, a missing selected file is created with no active targets and
an inert generated review queue. Without this option or its environment
equivalent, swarm-info uses a deployment-local or user-scoped default.
.TP
.BI \-\-remediation-plan-file " path"
Select the atomically written dry-run plan and sanitized execution record.
.TP
.B \-\-force-auto-remedy-attempt
Allow policy entries with
.B auto_eligible=false
to be attempted. This cannot bypass disabled entries, backup requirements,
repository/digest checks, candidate scans, source preconditions, confirmation,
convergence, post-validation, or rollback.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-runtime-override
Permit a separately confirmed
.B docker service update
fallback for an unresolved deployment source. This creates configuration drift
and remains disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-scan-vulnerabilities
Force a locked scan of every unique current Swarm service image. Add exactly
one of
.BR \-\-service ,
.BR \-\-image ,
or
.B \-\-stack
for a fresh focused verification of current live state.
.TP
.B \-\-compare-image-update
Scan one current and one proposed image, then report whether that concrete
candidate removes all, some, or none of the current fixable critical/high
findings. Each side is bound to an exact local image ID when installed, or an
immutable registry digest otherwise. Cross-repository candidates are accepted
for read-only evidence but never authorize deployment or prove compatibility.
.TP
.B \-\-discover-image-updates
Consume the existing schema-version-2 vulnerability report and discover
read-only update candidates. For strict stable X.Y.Z tags it selects the newest
same-minor, same-major, and overall stable releases; prereleases are not
ordered. Mutable latest receives only a latest-channel refresh. Selected tags
are resolved to immutable registry digests, using the requested platform for
platform-specific metadata, and aliases of the same artifact are merged. No
candidate is vulnerability-scanned or authorized for deployment by this
command.
.TP
.B \-\-assess-image-updates
Consume the Slice 1 candidate report and its exact schema-version-2 source
vulnerability report. Every immutable candidate is scanned once and reused
across consuming images and workload resources. Swarm evidence retains
per-service opportunities. Standalone evidence retains exact local image IDs,
affected containers, Compose ownership labels, current/candidate lineage, and
copy-ready backup, pull/build, recreate, verify, and focused-rescan commands.
Selection prioritizes critical findings removed, then high findings removed.
All commands are guidance only; compatibility and deployment remain unverified
and unauthorized.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow-registry-host " host"
With
.BR \-\-discover-image-updates ,
explicitly permit bounded anonymous metadata or token requests to one exact
host. Repeat for multiple hosts. A registry whose Bearer-token service uses a
different host reports that host as an additional required approval before
contacting it. Without this option discovery is network-silent and reports the
required hosts with exit status 3. Digest resolution uses public Registry V2
manifests and a temporary empty Docker configuration; installed registry
credentials are never read or sent, and image layers are not pulled.
.TP
.BI \-\-vulnerability-report-file " path"
Select the schema-version-2 source report consumed by
.BR \-\-discover-image-updates
or
.BR \-\-assess-image-updates .
Assessment defaults to the exact source path recorded by its candidate report;
an explicit path supports deliberately relocated evidence. Discovery defaults
to the preferred production vulnerability report when present.
.TP
.BI \-\-candidate-report-file " path"
Select the schema-version-1 candidate report consumed by
.BR \-\-assess-image-updates .
Default: the preferred production candidate report when present.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-registry-tags " count"
Bound tag enumeration per repository for
.BR \-\-discover-image-updates .
Range: 1 to 10000. Default: 10000. Hitting the limit leaves discovery
incomplete instead of guessing the newest tag.
.TP
.BI \-\-current-image " image"
With
.BR \-\-compare-image-update ,
select an arbitrary current local or registry image. Use this mode for
standalone Docker/QNAP and locally built images. It is mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-service .
.TP
.BI \-\-candidate-image " image"
Required with
.BR \-\-compare-image-update .
Select the concrete proposed local or registry image. Mutable tags are resolved
before scanning; the report records the exact artifact.
.TP
.BI \-\-service " name"
With
.BR \-\-scan-vulnerabilities ,
scan only the image currently specified by one exact live service name or ID.
With
.BR \-\-compare-image-update ,
use that live image as the current side of the comparison.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " reference"
With
.BR \-\-scan-vulnerabilities ,
scan one image used by current Swarm services. A tag may match its live
digest-pinned reference. If that tag maps to multiple live digests, supply one
exact image@digest instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-stack " name"
With
.BR \-\-scan-vulnerabilities ,
scan every current service in one exact Docker stack namespace, deduplicating
shared images.
.PP
Focused verification is manual-only, bypasses the full-report cache, and does
not replace or rotate the watchdog's all-service evidence. Without an explicit
output path it writes a separate
.I vulnerability_scan_focused.json
report.
.TP
.B \-\-security-check
Auto-detect manager capability. A manager receives Swarm-wide service-image
coverage; any other Docker host receives exact local-container image coverage.
The local mode is read-only, includes stopped containers by default, uses
Docker Scout
.B local://
only, and never substitutes a registry image. Interactive scans show inventory
totals, per-image counters and results, elapsed time, and a 30-second heartbeat
while Docker Scout remains active. A full local scan isolates unreadable
container metadata, retains readable image results, records inventory errors,
and returns incomplete status instead of reporting the host clean.
.PP
Compatibility checks bound Docker Scout to 45 minutes per image and four hours
of aggregate image work by default. A timeout or exhausted budget is recorded
as incomplete evidence. Completed image entries include their scan duration.
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime-mode " mode"
Set security inventory to
.BR auto ,
.BR swarm ,
or
.BR containers .
Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-container-mode
Alias for
.BR "\-\-runtime-mode containers" .
.TP
.BI \-\-container-scope " scope"
Select
.B all
defined local containers or only
.BR running .
Default: all.
.TP
.BI \-\-container " name"
With
.BR \-\-security-check ,
scan the exact local image used by one exact container name or full container
ID. This selects local-container mode automatically. Without an explicit output
path, focused evidence is written separately and does not replace the full-host
report. The focused check inspects only that container, so unrelated unreadable
stopped containers do not block verification.
.TP
.BI \-\-image-id " sha256:id"
With
.BR \-\-security-check ,
scan one full content-addressed local image ID and report every selected
container using that exact artifact. Abbreviated IDs and tags are rejected.
This selects local-container mode automatically and asks Docker to filter the
candidate containers before exact identity is verified.
.TP
.BI \-\-compose-project " project"
With
.BR \-\-security-check ,
scan every container whose exact
.B com.docker.compose.project
label matches the selected project. This selects local-container mode and
writes separate focused evidence.
.TP
.BI \-\-compose-service " project/service"
With
.BR \-\-security-check ,
scan every container whose exact Compose project and service labels match the
selected pair. Missing or ambiguous selector parts are rejected; no container
name or path guessing is performed.
.TP
.BI \-\-os " host"
Use host hint
.BR auto ,
.BR qnap ,
or
.BR linux .
Default: auto. The hint changes metadata and guidance but never bypasses
Docker capability checks.
.TP
.TP
.B \-\-container-state
Publish private, atomic operational evidence for all local containers without
invoking Docker Scout or interpreting watchdog policy.
.TP
.B \-\-scheduled-container-state
Run the same cheap collector used by the managed five-minute schedule.
.TP
.BI \-\-freshness-minutes " minutes"
Set the operational evidence freshness window. Default: 15.
.B \-\-scheduled-vulnerability-scan
Run the locked scan unless matching evidence is fresh.
.TP
.B \-\-scheduled-security-check
Run or reuse the locked local-container security check. The scheduled default
scope is running containers.
.TP
.B \-\-vulnerability-status
Check report completeness and freshness without Docker Scout.
.TP
.B \-\-security-status
Check local-container report completeness and freshness without Docker Scout.
.TP
.B \-\-install-vulnerability-cron
Install or update the current user's managed daily scan.
.TP
.B \-\-install-security-cron
Install or update a managed five-minute operational collector and daily
running-container security check. The default 72-hour cache interval avoids a
full Scout run every day. On QNAP,
run this installation once with sudo and
.B \-\-cron-runtime-user
so swarm-info updates /etc/config/crontab persistently, reloads cron, and runs
the actual scan as the named non-root account.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-vulnerability-cron
Remove only the managed daily scan block.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-security-cron
Remove only the managed container-security block.
.TP
.BI \-\-platform " platform"
Set the scan platform. Swarm scan default: linux/amd64. Compatibility security
check default: auto-detect from the Docker daemon.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-age-hours " hours"
Set the evidence freshness limit. Swarm default: 30; container schedule: 96.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache-age-hours " hours"
Set the scheduled rescan interval. Swarm default: 20; container schedule: 72.
.TP
.BI \-\-history-days " days"
Set vulnerability report retention. Default: 14.
.TP
.BI \-\-lock-file " path"
Override the vulnerability job lock file.
.TP
.BI \-\-cron-hour " hour"
Set the daily scan hour. Default: 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-cron-minute " minute"
Set the daily scan minute. Default: 17.
.TP
.BI \-\-cron-log-file " path"
Set the optional scheduled-scan log destination.
.TP
.BI \-\-scout-timeout-minutes " minutes"
Set the maximum duration of one Scout image command. Container-job default: 45.
.TP
.BI \-\-scan-budget-minutes " minutes"
Set the aggregate image-scanning budget. Container-job default: 240.
.TP
.BI \-\-cron-runtime-user " user"
Set the non-root account used by a persistent QNAP system cron entry. This
account must own the Docker Scout installation and Docker credentials.
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-menu
Open context navigation after a single page.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fast
Run the complete tour without waiting between pages.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait
Run the complete tour with page waits.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Fetch and apply only a clean, strict fast-forward update.
.TP
.B \-\-check-dependencies
Auto-detect and check full Swarm-manager readiness or the narrower portable
Docker/Python/Scout readiness without requiring Swarm, Git, bc, or Compose.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the authoritative swarm-info version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Healthy/clean evidence or a successful operational action.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid input, unavailable core dependency, or operational failure.
.TP
.B 2
The requested operator report requires attention, or deployment mapping found
unknown or ambiguous services.
.TP
.B 3
Vulnerability evidence is missing, incomplete, stale, or unavailable; or image
cleanup, image update discovery, or image update assessment could not establish
or complete its requested safe operation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /info_json/swarm_info.json
Preferred production health report.
.TP
.I /info_json/vulnerability_scan.json
Preferred production vulnerability report.
.TP
.I /info_json/vulnerability_scan_focused.json
Preferred focused service, image, or stack verification report. It never
replaces the all-service watchdog report by default.
.TP
.I /info_json/image_update_comparison.json
Preferred atomic current-versus-candidate image comparison. It is independent
from the all-service watchdog report and never authorizes deployment.
.TP
.I /info_json/image_update_candidates.json
Preferred atomic read-only image candidate and lifecycle evidence report. The
report records exact registry approvals and immutable digests but contains no
deployment authorization or candidate vulnerability verdict.
.TP
.I /info_json/image_update_assessment.json
Preferred atomic batch candidate-scan report. It contains global and
per-service verified update reductions while explicitly withholding
compatibility proof and deployment authorization.
.TP
.I .../swarm-info/container_state.json
Adapter-owned raw local-container state, written every five minutes and fresh
for 15 minutes by default.
.TP
.I .../swarm-info/security_scan-running.status.json
Atomic scan phase, image counter, 30-second heartbeat, last-complete time, and
next-run evidence. It never replaces the last complete vulnerability report.
.TP
.I swarm_info/security_scan.json
Default standalone/QNAP compatibility security report. It is separate from
watchdog evidence.
.TP
.I swarm_info/security_scan_focused.json
Default focused container or exact-local-image verification report. It does
not replace the full standalone/QNAP report.
.TP
.I /info_json/service_deployment_map.json
Suggested path for an explicitly generated deployment-map acceptance report.
.TP
.I /info_json/vulnerability_remediation_plan.json
Default atomic remediation dry-run and sanitized execution record when the
directory is writable.
.TP
.I config/remediation-policy.example.json
Empty schema-3 policy template. Its optional successor mappings influence only
read-only image discovery. A pre-existing file is optional because a safe
run can create an installation-owned policy and generated review queue.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swarm-info/remediation-policy.json
Default user-scoped policy and generated review queue outside a Git deployment
repository with an existing
.I configs/
directory. XDG_CONFIG_HOME changes the configuration base.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/swarm-info.1
User-installed manual page.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWARM_INFO_DEPLOY_ROOTS
Path-separated default deployment roots used when
.B \-\-deploy-root
is absent. Default: /swarm.
.TP
.B SWARM_INFO_REMEDIATION_POLICY
Default installation-owned remediation policy path. An explicit
.B \-\-remediation-policy
value takes precedence. A missing selected path is created only when automatic
remediation is entered.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration base used for a generated user-scoped remediation policy.
Default: ~/.config.
.TP
.B SWARM_INFO_LOCALE
Set to a value beginning with
.B de
for German operator output; otherwise English is used.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Existing values are preserved. On QNAP, security checks otherwise use the
private data-volume-backed directory
.I ~/.cache/swarm-info/docker-scout/tmp
instead of the capacity-limited system temporary directory.
.TP
.B DOCKER_SCOUT_CACHE_DIR
Existing values are preserved. On QNAP, security checks otherwise use
.I ~/.cache/swarm-info/docker-scout/cache
for Docker Scout cache data.
.TP
.B SWARM_INFO_SECURITY_REPORT_FILE
Explicit full standalone/QNAP report used by
.BR "swarm-info \-v" .
Without it, standard QNAP public paths and then the checkout-local security
report are discovered automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
Verify service-to-stack mappings without changing the Swarm:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --map-service-deployments --deploy-root /swarm --output-file /info_json/service_deployment_map.json
.fi
.PP
Show the current vulnerability evidence:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info -v
.fi
.PP
Review required registry hosts without sending repository metadata:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --discover-image-updates \
  --output-file /info_json/image_update_candidates.json
.fi
.PP
Discover public Docker Hub and GHCR candidates after reviewing those hosts:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --discover-image-updates --allow-registry-host docker.io \
  --allow-registry-host ghcr.io \
  --output-file /info_json/image_update_candidates.json
.fi
.PP
Scan each discovered immutable candidate once and calculate verified update
reductions:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --assess-image-updates \
  --candidate-report-file /info_json/image_update_candidates.json \
  --output-file /info_json/image_update_assessment.json
.fi
.PP
Verify one service after redeploying its remediated image:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --scan-vulnerabilities --service my-stack_api
.fi
.PP
Verify one exact live image or all images in one stack:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --scan-vulnerabilities --image nginx:1.27
swarm-info --scan-vulnerabilities --stack my-stack
.fi
.PP
Prove the security effect of a proposed replacement for one live service:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --compare-image-update --service my-stack_api \
  --candidate-image registry.example/my-app:2.0
.fi
.PP
Compare an image you built locally without pushing it first:
.PP
.nf
docker build -t my-app:security-candidate .
swarm-info --compare-image-update --current-image my-app:current \
  --candidate-image my-app:security-candidate
.fi
.PP
Scan exact images used by local QNAP containers:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --security-check --container-mode --os=qnap \
  --output-file /share/Public/swarm-info/security_scan.json
.fi
.PP
Install the bounded running-container schedule on QNAP:
.PP
.nf
sudo "$(command -v swarm-info)" --install-security-cron --os=qnap \
  --cron-runtime-user "$(id -un)" \
  --output-file /share/Public/swarm-info/security_scan-running.json
.fi
.PP
Recheck one recreated QNAP container without replacing the full report:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --security-check \
  --container docker-wordpress-nginx-telegram_homepage-1 --os=qnap
.fi
.PP
Recheck one exact local image artifact and all containers using it:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --security-check \
  --image-id sha256:<64-hex-digits> --os=qnap
.fi
.PP
Review unused images on the current Docker node without deleting:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info -i
.fi
.PP
Review again and request default-No confirmation before removal:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info -i --apply
.fi
.PP
Run conservative remediation without preparing a policy first:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --remediate-vulnerabilities --deploy-root /swarm
.fi
.PP
Keep generated review evidence and explicit overrides in a deployment repo:
.PP
.nf
swarm-info --remediate-vulnerabilities --deploy-root /swarm \
  --remediation-policy /swarm/administration/swarm-info-watchdog/configs/remediation-policy.json
.fi
